 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "PersistentKVStore() starts empty. set(key, value) stores or overwrites; get(key) returns the value or \"\" when absent; delete(key) returns whether a key was removed. save() returns the blob of the current state. The blob is the magic bytes 80, 75, 86, 50 (\"PKV2\"), then a body in the level-1 layout, then a 4-byte big-endian checksum equal to the sum of the body bytes modulo 2**32. The body is a list of byte values 0..255: a 4-byte big-endian entry count, then for each entry in ascending key order a 4-byte big-endian key length, the key's ASCII bytes, a 4-byte big-endian value length and the value's ASCII bytes. load(blob) returns true and replaces the state when the blob is well formed; it returns false and leaves the state unchanged when the magic, any length, the checksum, the key order (strictly ascending), the key alphabet [a-z0-9]{1,10} or the value alphabet (printable ASCII, 1 to 20) is wrong, or when bytes are missing or left over. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
